kind how-do-i
title How do I give a display a label of my own?
intro A label is a name you give a display or an input device, which the Flow tab shows in place of its connector or its device name. The label waits for Save like any other change.
see heads-and-rules/show-a-terminal-on-a-display

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
device display HDMI-A-1 GSM:0x5b88:LEFT0001

1. Go to the Flow tab.
2. Choose HDMI-A-1.
3. Choose Label.
4. Type Left screen.
5. Press Enter.
at the label
check screen lacks "wrote it to the draft"
check screen shows "Press Esc and then s to save it into the draft."
6. Press Esc.
7. Press s to save.
check draft has "Left screen"
